# 📊 N100 Sprint 2 – Financial Ratio Engine

A production-style financial analytics engine built for computing **50+ financial KPIs** across **92 companies over multiple years**.  
This project processes raw financial statements and transforms them into structured, decision-ready financial intelligence.

---

## 🚀 Project Objective

To build a **scalable financial ratio engine** that:

- Computes profitability, leverage, efficiency, and cash flow KPIs
- Handles real-world financial edge cases (negative equity, debt-free firms, etc.)
- Generates growth metrics using CAGR models
- Produces structured datasets for financial analysis

---

## 🧠 Key Features

### 📌 1. Profitability Ratios
- Net Profit Margin
- Operating Profit Margin
- Return on Equity (ROE)
- Return on Assets (ROA)
- Return on Capital Employed (ROCE)

---

### 📌 2. Leverage & Efficiency Metrics
- Debt-to-Equity Ratio
- Interest Coverage Ratio
- Net Debt Calculation
- Asset Turnover Ratio
- High Leverage Flagging System

---

### 📌 3. Cash Flow Analytics
- Free Cash Flow (FCF)
- CFO Quality Score
- CapEx Intensity Classification
- FCF Conversion Rate
- Capital Allocation Pattern Detection (8 business patterns)

---

### 📌 4. Growth Engine (CAGR)
- Revenue CAGR (3Y / 5Y / 10Y)
- PAT CAGR (3Y / 5Y / 10Y)
- EPS CAGR (3Y / 5Y / 10Y)

Includes edge-case handling:
- Turnaround companies
- Negative-to-positive transitions
- Zero-base scenarios
- Insufficient data handling

